course: dictionary
lesson: 13730
title: Intended: planned or meant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When something is intended, it was planned, or it was meant for a certain purpose or person. «I intended to call you after school.» That means I planned to call you. Intended is the past form of the verb intend.
explain: Read the words around it to find the meaning. «The game is intended for children aged 8 and up.» The words about children aged 8 and up tell you who the game was made for, so intended means meant for that group.
explain: Try swapping in a simple word, like planned or meant, and check that the sentence still makes sense. «The rain was not intended to spoil our picnic» means the rain was not planned to spoil it.
fact: Intended means planned or meant.
fact: Intended is the past form of the verb intend: intend, intends, intended, intending.
fact: «Intended for» means made or meant for a particular person or use, as on a label: «intended for ages 6+».
fact: «As intended» means just as it was planned.
fact: Old-fashioned: someone's intended is the person they plan to marry.
exercise: «The sign said the play area was intended for younger children.» What does intended mean here? | Lost by | *Meant for | Painted in | Afraid of
exercise: «I intended to finish my homework before tea, but I forgot.» What does intended mean here? | Dropped | *Planned | Finished | Forgotten
exercise: «The toy box says it is intended for ages 6+.» Find and copy the word that is the past form of intend. | ages | toy | *intended | says
test: «The trip went exactly as intended.» What does as intended mean? | Much faster than expected | Cancelled at the last minute | Without any help | *Just as it was planned
test: «Mum intended to bake a cake, but the oven broke.» What does intended mean here? | Was lucky enough to | Forgot to | Refused to | *Planned to
exam: «The new park is intended for families, so it has benches and a picnic area.» What does intended mean in this sentence? | *Meant for families | Old and broken | Closed for repairs | Built by accident
